title: Denial Intelligence › Ways in
route: /denials
intro: Every way a person lands on Denial Intelligence, how the address picks the denial that opens first, and how the sidebar badge counts open denials.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'Denial Intelligence' in the sidebar"
start s2 "Demo menu, Suggested path\n'Denial Intelligence: D-3318'"
start s3 "Click a notification\n'Denied today', 'Denied', 'Partly approved' or 'Denial analyzed'"
start s4 "Ask FLO about denials or money\nClick 'Open Denial Intelligence'"
start s5 "Analytics: 'Common denial reasons by payer'\nClick a row or its payer name\n(the address carries that payer and reason)"
start s6 "Dashboard request drawer\nClick 'Open in Denial Intelligence'"
start s7 "Authorizations case page, banner 'This request was denied'\nClick 'Open in Denial Intelligence'"

process p1 "Address is /denials or /denials?id=D-xxxx"
decision d1 "Is there an ?id= in the address?"
decision d2 "Is it an open denial, or one closed on this screen?"
decision d3 "Are there any open denials?"
process p2 "Pick the first denial in the list: the nearest deadline\n(among the matches, when filters are on)"
process p3 "Show the denial named in the address"
toast t1 "'We could not find D-xxxx among the open denials'\n'Showing D-3318 instead.' (the first in the list)"

screen sc1 "Denial Intelligence\nHeader, 'Add a denial letter', the denial, 'Open denials' list"
screen sc2 "'No open denials'\n'Everything sent is approved or waiting. Add a denial letter above to analyze a new one.'"
click c1 "Click 'Open the Dashboard'"

goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Open denials list"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened"
goto g3 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Add a denial letter"
goto g4 "Continues in: Dashboard › Arrive › What the page shows"
process pf "The address may also carry ?payer= and ?reason=\nThey narrow the 'Open denials' list only; ?id= still works"
goto g5 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Open denials list › Filter by payer and reason"
screen sc3 "'No open denials match these filters'\nbutton 'Clear filters'"

start s8 "Look at the badge beside 'Denial Intelligence' in the sidebar"
process b1 "Badge = requests in the Dashboard's 'Appeal or call' stage\n8 at the start"
process b2 "Goes up by one: a letter is analyzed, or the Dashboard demo control 'Denies' or 'Approves part' is used"
process b3 "Goes down by one: the denial is accepted, a call outcome 'Overturned' or 'Partly restored' is logged, or the payer's decision on an appeal is 'Overturned' or 'Partly overturned'"

s1 --> p1
p1 -.-> pf --> g5
pf -.->|Nothing matches| sc3
s2 --> p1
s3 --> p1
s4 --> p1
s5 --> p1
s6 --> p1
s7 --> p1
p1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| d3
d1 -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Yes| p3 --> sc1
d2 -->|No, unknown id| d3
d3 -->|Yes| p2 --> sc1
p2 -.->|if the id was unknown| t1 -.-> sc1
d3 -->|No| sc2
sc2 --> c1 --> g4
sc2 --> g3
sc1 --> g1 & g2

s8 --> b1 --> b2 & b3
